//< Sema clearly rejects a direct `::` value cast to a struct type
//<
//< Let through, a cast from a scalar or another struct becomes the invalid C `(StructType)value`
//< (see ksplc/sema/body/postfix.kspls). A source type implementing operator.Cast (`ci.Ci32::10`)
//< resolves to a cast() call and passes, so Ci32 to Ci64, with no Cast, is used here.
// EXPECT: cannot cast to struct type
import "std/checked_int" as ci

fn main()
  a: = ci.Ci32.new(10)
  b: = ci.Ci64::a
